---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MediaCredit from "../components/MediaCredit.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---
<Layout title={`Accessibility & media credits — ${site.wordmark}`}>
  <div class="reading-container">
    <header class="page-title"><h1>Accessibility & media credits</h1><p class="lead">The design target is WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA.</p><p>Automated checks support this research site's accessibility work; they do not establish complete ADA or WCAG conformance.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <section><h2>Using this site</h2><ul>
        <li>The first keyboard link skips to the main content. Focus is visible and the layout reflows on narrow screens.</li>
        <li>Silent videos play when visible. Each native player provides keyboard-operable play and pause controls. A manual pause is remembered when you scroll away and return.</li>
        <li>Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences prevent automatic playback. Native controls still let you choose to play. Moving a video out of view or hiding the tab pauses it.</li>
        <li>The opening video has no audio track. It fills the width of the screen and may crop slightly on very tall or wide windows. A complete text alternative and a timed visual description accompany it.</li>
        <li>Images have descriptive alternatives. Labels and text carry their meaning; the red-to-green bar in the background figure is decorative, and color alone is not required.</li>
        <li>Core research content and native media controls remain available without JavaScript. The citation can be selected as text.</li>
      </ul></section>
      <section><h2>Media scope and sources</h2><p>The homepage follows the authors’ proposal defense presentation: background, methodology, experiment, results, and conclusion. The two result charts are panels a–b of Figure 2 and Figure 3 of the published paper, as shown on slides 21–22; each has alternative text and a full text description, including the network values from the paper’s tables. In the per-intersection chart, blue and red are also named in the chart’s legend and in the description. The opening city traffic video is a rendering from slide 14; it illustrates urban traffic and is not a recording of the study’s simulation or controller.</p></section>
      <section id="attachments"><h2>Paper and research materials</h2><p>The <a href={site.paperUrl}>published paper</a> provides the complete study. A <a href={site.htmlPaper}>full preprint in HTML</a> is also available; it is a preprint version, not a guaranteed identical copy of the published article.</p><p>The supplied publisher PDF is untagged and remains unchanged. External PDFs have not been fully assessed for tags, reading order, mathematical accessibility, or assistive-technology behavior. Original research data are preserved in the repository; the website presents a concise overview with the key results.</p><p>All homepage images come from the authors' proposal defense presentation; see the <a href={`${asset()}#method`}>methodology</a> and the sources below. Rights in third-party media remain with their respective holders.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Checks and remaining review</h2><p>The deployment workflow includes axe-core checks against WCAG 2.1 A/AA rules, keyboard navigation, native media controls, reduced-motion and data-saving behavior, image alternatives, narrow-screen reflow, text spacing, and content without JavaScript. See the <a href={`${site.siteRepo}/actions`}>deployment checks</a>.</p><p>Screen-reader usability, scientific image contrast, external attachments, and review with users with disabilities require further assessment. This site does not claim an ADA or WCAG certification.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Report an access barrier</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:liusongyang@ufl.edu">Songyang Liu at liusongyang@ufl.edu</a> with the page, content needed, browser, and assistive technology involved.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Privacy</h2><p>This static site serves its fonts, figures, and video locally, without analytics or embedded third-party players. External links open the provider's site, where its privacy practices apply.</p></section>
    </div>
    <div class="section"><MediaCredit /></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
